From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Henrik Klee <henrik@goat-code.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 23:44:44 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: display: apple,s8000-display-pipe: Allow a MIPI
 DSI panel link

The A9 iPhones drive their panel over MIPI DSI (Apple device tree
mipi-dsim), not eDP: their pipe holds the mipi_dsi power domain and has
no DisplayPort transmitter. Describe the A9 pipe's second power domain
as the panel link, as the A8's already is, and its "dp" window as
present on eDP boards only.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 .../bindings/display/apple,s8000-display-pipe.yaml        | 8 ++++++--
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/display/apple,s8000-display-pipe.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/display/apple,s8000-display-pipe.yaml
index ae952597..20fbd86a 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/display/apple,s8000-display-pipe.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/display/apple,s8000-display-pipe.yaml
@@ -194,7 +194,9 @@ allOf:
             - description: Seven-register side block
             - description: Display DART (dart-disp0), first window
             - description: Display DART (dart-disp0), second window
-            - description: DisplayPort transmitter (displayport)
+            - description:
+                DisplayPort transmitter (displayport), on the boards whose
+                panel link is eDP
 
         reg-names:
           minItems: 6
@@ -222,7 +224,9 @@ allOf:
         power-domains:
           items:
             - description: Display pipe (disp0)
-            - description: DisplayPort/eDP controller (dp)
+            - description:
+                Panel link the bootloader left running, MIPI DSI (mipi_dsi)
+                or DisplayPort (dp)
 
 required:
   - compatible
